From 744ac50846c697afffec146710365547fba99cf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:42:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban restart resume: plan and copy off the owner
 loop, fail-soft; skip rotated sessions; 15% headroom

Review fixes: planning (transcript read, token estimate, context-length lookup that may
probe over HTTP) now runs in the tracked off-loop write with the copy, after session
creation, so the owner loop never blocks on it and the saved-claim/create invariant is
untouched. Any exception is a recorded fallback (plan_failed / seed_failed), never an
admission failure. A prior session ended by rotation compaction falls back
(prior_session_rotated). Resume only below 85% of the owner's compaction threshold, for
the first turn and owner/worker context-length lookup differences.
